    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d705">

                <pb facs="0655" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/10897: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-30T11:00:00+09:00">October 30, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 30—2:11 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>502. Department’s 273, October 29, 1 p.m.<anchor n="80" xml:id="d705-f1"/>
                    Discreet approach reveals that the German Embassy has received no information
                    that any discussion of the character suggested by the Associated Press despatch
                    has taken place between the German and Japanese Ambassadors in China. It is also
                    revealed that the relations between the two <pb facs="0656" n="649"
                        xml:id="pg649"/> Ambassadors had not been “very satisfactory” owing to the
                    employment by China of German military instructors and also to Japanese
                    suspicion that Trautmann<anchor n="81" xml:id="d705-f2"/> is “pro-Chinese” and
                    that Trautmann took advantage of a recent visit to Shanghai to improve his
                    relations with Kawagoe<anchor n="82" xml:id="d705-f3"/> (see our 464, October 9,
                    9 p.m.).</p>
                <p>The German Military Attaché is to return from Shanghai and the German Embassy has
                    offered to give us any further information on this matter which he may
                    bring.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
